"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"What industries do you serve?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"We serve electrical contractors, civil contractors, water and sewer utilities (including HRSD), telecom companies, municipalities, and engineering firms. Our precision excavation services are trusted for fiber optic installation, power line work, utility upgrades, and infrastructure verification projects.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Is hydro excavation safer than traditional excavation?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes, hydro excavation is significantly safer than mechanical excavation. It eliminates the risk of utility strikes that can cause injuries, service outages, and expensive repairs. The non-destructive nature protects gas lines, electrical cables, fiber optics, and water mains during excavation.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Can you work in cold weather?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes, hydro excavation works effectively in cold weather and frozen ground conditions when traditional excavation methods struggle. Our heated water systems can break through frost and frozen soil, making it ideal for year-round utility work in the Mid-Atlantic region.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How do I get a quote?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Contact us at 757-510-5220 or email info@beachhydrovac.com for a free quote. We will discuss your project requirements, timeline, and provide competitive pricing. As a veteran-owned local business, we pride ourselves on responsive service and fair pricing.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</script>\n<!-- /wp:html -->"}